  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Scrub sweet potatoes, cut deep slit in top of each, place on cookie sheet, put into oven preheated to 375 degrees F, bake 1 hour, until tender when pierced with fork.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, cut baby carrots into 1 inch pieces, place into saucepan, add water to cover, 1 tablespoon sugar, 2 tablespoons butter, salt and pepper. Cook uncovered about 30 minutes until water is mostly evaporated and carrots are tender to fork.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Scrape potato out of skins and combine with carrots in bowl of food processor, fitted with steel blade. Gradually add half & half and process until smooth, creamy consistency is attained.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add nutmeg, orange zest, orange juice, 2 tablespoons of brown sugar, ginger, salt and pepper. Once mixed, transfer to pot on stove, set to simmer. Add 9 tablespoons of butter, (reserving 1 tablespoon for pecans). Once completely heated, transfer to oven/microwave-proof baking dish.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Top with pecans, pan-toasted in 1 tablespoon butter, with 1 tablespoon brown sugar, and dashes of salt and cayenne.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "For timeliness with serving schedule, keep covered and warm in 350 degree oven until time to serve. 6-8 portions. All amounts of ingredients can be modified, according to taste.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
